  {
    "sha": "25cf76ef36d25a3ba005b924391bed7aad2fadc3",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVDa2Y9oAKDI1Y2Y3NmVmMzZkMjVhM2JhMDA1YjkyNDM5MWJlZDdhYWQyZmFkYzM",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "yibie",
        "email": "yibie@outlook.com",
        "date": "2026-10-10T04:15:54Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "yibie",
        "email": "yibie@outlook.com",
        "date": "2026-10-10T04:15:54Z"
      },
      "message": "Prompts: experts multiplied from the file's blocks a tile at a time, every type (IQ3_S 352-379 -> 633-649 tok/s)\n\ntile_matmul: a threadgroup unpacks 64 rows by 64 columns of a tile's expert into its own memory and Apple's\nmatmul2d multiplies the tile's 16 tokens by that. One product of 10,220 pairs takes 4.5-5.4 ms whatever the\ntype. It replaces the 2-bit operand with its split and sums (Q2_0: a layer 22 -> 16 ms) and the stacks unpacked\nto 1.7 GB of floats for gather_mm (the IQ3_S file: 43-79 -> 16 ms).\n\nA piece of 1,024 tokens: Q2_0 648-679 tok/s, IQ3_S 633-649. The comparison's prompt of 1,180 tokens with the\ndraft head: 555-560 and 488-513 (llama.cpp 494 and 488). Agreement with llama.cpp's answers as before or\nbetter; float32 and the paged mode checked. 256 tests.",
