      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "yibie",
        "email": "yibie@outlook.com",
        "date": "2026-10-10T03:24:15Z"
      },
      "message": "Prompts: the pairs are sorted by expert on the GPU, and a chunk no longer stops at every layer (376 -> 559 tok/s)\n\nMeasured before building a new product kernel (e31, e32): the 2-bit product already ran at what MLX's own\ngrouped products reach (7 T operations a second); a chunk of 1,024 tokens paid 1.7-2.1 s for 1.0 s of experts\nbecause sorting the pairs on the CPU made the pass wait at every layer for the routers' choice. tiles_of lays\nthe tiles out with array operations, as many as the pairs could need at most; the kernel skips the unused.\n\nA prompt of 1,180 tokens: 2.3 s (514 tok/s) where it took 2.9-3.1. Agreement with llama.cpp unchanged.",
